# BugLens

[![QA Pipeline](BADGE_URL)](ACTIONS_URL)

**Live Demo:** https://buglence.vercel.app/

### AI-Powered QA Assistant for Requirement Analysis, Bug Reporting, and Test Design

BugLens is an AI-powered QA assistant designed to help QA Engineers analyze software requirements, transform raw issue descriptions into structured bug reports, generate professional test cases, and receive AI-assisted QA insights.

The project follows a simple principle: **AI Recommendation + Human Validation**. AI provides recommendations and structured analysis, while the QA Engineer remains responsible for validation and final decisions.

## Core Features

### Requirement Analyzer

BugLens analyzes software requirements from a QA perspective and helps identify **ambiguities, missing information, potential risks, suggested test scenarios, and edge cases** before testing begins.

### Bug Report Generator

Raw issue descriptions can be transformed into structured bug reports containing the **title, preconditions, steps to reproduce, expected result, actual result, severity, priority, and environment information**.

### AI-Powered QA Insights

QA Engineers can optionally request AI recommendations for **severity, priority, possible root causes, suggested fixes, regression scope, confidence score, and reasoning summary**. These insights are recommendations intended to support investigation rather than replace QA judgement.

### Test Case Generator

BugLens generates structured **Positive, Negative, Edge Case, and Regression test cases**. Generated cases can include preconditions, execution steps, expected results, severity, and priority.

### Export & Integration

Generated QA artifacts can be copied for **Jira and Azure DevOps**, exported as JSON, or copied directly for use in existing QA workflows.

# Architecture

BugLens uses a modern web architecture consisting of **React, Vite, and Tailwind CSS** on the frontend and **Node.js with Express.js** on the backend.

The AI layer uses LLM-powered generation services with structured JSON responses, validation, and normalization to produce predictable outputs that can be consumed by the application.

text

Frontend
React + Vite + Tailwind CSS
        │
        ▼
Backend
Node.js + Express.js
        │
        ▼
AI Services
LLM Generation + JSON Validation


# Quality Engineering

BugLens is not only an AI application; the project also includes an end-to-end QA implementation covering **Manual Testing, API Testing, UI Automation, Regression Testing, and Continuous Integration**.

The testing strategy validates the application at both API and UI levels while keeping automated regression coverage integrated into the development workflow.

## API Testing

API testing is implemented using **Postman and Newman**. The current regression collection contains **12 API requests** covering the Requirement Analyzer, Bug Report Generator, and Test Case Generator.

The API suite covers happy paths, negative scenarios, missing required fields, invalid inputs, HTTP status codes, JSON responses, response structures, data types, and validation errors.

### Run API Tests

Install Newman and execute the collection:

bash

npm install -g newman
newman run postman/BugLense.postman_collection.json


# UI Test Automation

UI regression automation is implemented using **Java 17, Selenium WebDriver, TestNG, Maven, and Page Object Model (POM)**.

The current automation suite contains **23 Selenium regression tests** covering the three core BugLens workflows: Requirement Analyzer, Bug Report Generator, and Test Case Generator.

The Page Object Model separates page interactions from test logic to keep the automation framework maintainable and scalable.

### Run Selenium Regression

bash

mvn -f automation/pom.xml test -DbaseUrl="https://buglence.vercel.app/"


Test execution reports are generated inside:

text

automation/target/surefire-reports/


# Continuous Integration

BugLens uses **GitHub Actions** to automatically execute API and UI regression tests.

Every push to the `main` branch can trigger both the **Postman API Regression Suite** and the **Selenium UI Regression Suite**. The workflow can also be triggered manually when regression execution is required.

text

GitHub Actions
      │
      ├── Postman / Newman API Tests
      │
      └── Selenium / TestNG UI Tests


This allows application changes to receive automated regression feedback without manually executing the complete test suites.

